## Residual notes (non-blocking)

1. The `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` parenthetical in plan D4/phase-02 slightly misdescribes semantics: a no-target `DO NOTHING` *silently skips* collisions on either unique — it does not "surface drift as an error". If drift-surfacing is actually desired, use `ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING` (errors on the `(namespace, chain_reference)` unique); otherwise fix the comment. For fixed seed values the silent-skip is acceptable — the integration test asserts the `code` rows exist, so drift is caught downstream anyway. Cosmetic.
2. Phase-02's Architecture paragraph still asserts "unreachable by construction" without noting the claim only holds post-D4b. Cosmetic — the Requirements section above it makes the dependency clear.

